# Normalise line endings to LF everywhere, including in Windows working
# copies.
#
# Without this, `core.autocrlf=true` (the Git for Windows default, and what
# is set on the machine this was built on) checks these files out with CRLF.
# That matters here because the Dockerfiles COPY straight from the working
# copy into Linux images: a shell script or an nginx include carrying \r
# fails inside the container with errors that point nowhere useful.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files must never be touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
